## SQ-CFR-01 | campfire rain mixin applies once, from Delight
@group A
@commands Boot; `grep -n "CampfireRainMixin" logs/debug.log`; `grep -niE "campfire.*(error\|exception)\|InvalidInjection" logs/latest.log \| head`
@pass `CampfireRainMixin` applies once, from `creativedelight.mixins.json` (none from `creativecompat.mixins.json`); no injection error (CD has `defaultRequire: 1`, so a miss crashes the boot)
@fails Mixin json entry, or a stale Compat jar still listing it (applied twice: `@Unique` field clash)
@from batches/r1106spf/b1.qb
shell grep -c "CampfireRainMixin" logs/debug.log; grep -n "CampfireRainMixin" logs/debug.log | head -3; grep -niE "campfire.*(error|exception)|InvalidInjection" logs/latest.log | head
bootreject (?i)campfire.*(InvalidInjection|exception)
look one apply, from creativedelight.mixins.json

## SQ-CFR-02
@group A
@commands Before the boot: `config/creativecompat-common.toml` holds `[campfire]` with `rainOutTicks = 100`, `config/creativedelight-common.toml` exists without `[campfire]`. Boot; read both files; reboot and grep again
@pass `[swaps] config sections [campfire] merged from creativecompat-common.toml into creativedelight-common.toml`; the CD file has `[campfire]` with `rainOutTicks = 100` and the other six keys; after the boot the Compat file has no `[campfire]`; second boot: no merge line, no WARN
@fails `CreativeDelight` constructor order (carry must run before `registerConfig`), or Forge did not correct the Compat file
@reviewed 2026-11-16
bootexpect \[swaps\] config sections \[campfire\] merged from creativecompat-common\.toml into creativedelight-common\.toml
shell grep -A9 "^\[campfire\]" config/creativedelight-common.toml | grep -E "^\s*\w+ =" | cut -c1-100
shell grep -A9 "^\[campfire\]" config/creativedelight-common.toml | grep -qE "^\s*rainOutTicks = 100" && test "$(grep -A9 '^\[campfire\]' config/creativedelight-common.toml | grep -cE '^\s*\w+ =')" -ge 7 && echo "CD [campfire] carried, 7 keys"
shell ! grep -q "^\[campfire\]" config/creativecompat-common.toml && echo "Compat file has no [campfire]"
look own boot with the Commands cell's two files written before it; the second boot (same srv): no merge line and no WARN naming campfire (bootreject on that boot)
## SQ-CFR-03 | [campfire] carried from Compat's file into a new CD file, then the CD carve tables merged from the old file
@group A
@commands Before the boot: no `config/creativedelight-common.toml`; Compat file with `[campfire] rainOutTicks = 100`. Boot
@pass `[swaps] config sections [campfire] carried over from creativecompat-common.toml to creativedelight-common.toml`, then the CD carve sections merged from `creativeengineering-common.toml` (if present); the CD file has `[members]`, `[campfire]` (100) and every other section after Forge's correction
@fails `carrySections` wrote the file first and the second carry skipped: the merge branch must run
@from batches/r1113/c2_l2.qb
bootexpect \[swaps\] config sections \[campfire\] carried over from creativecompat-common.toml to creativedelight-common.toml
bootexpect \[swaps\] config sections \[crop_growth, dandelion_maturing, crop_drops, stem_fruit, canning, cooking, perf\] merged from creativeengineering-common.toml into creativedelight-common.toml
bootreject could not (carry|merge) config sections
shell grep -nE "^\[" config/creativedelight-common.toml | tr '\n' ' '; echo; grep -nE "rainOutTicks *=" config/creativedelight-common.toml; grep -cE "^\[campfire\]" config/creativecompat-common.toml; true
look the carry line comes before the merge line in the log; the CD file has [members] (or [compartments], M8), [campfire] with rainOutTicks = 100 and every other section after Forge's correction; last number 0 = Forge dropped [campfire] from Compat's file

## SQ-CFR-04 | a pack that skipped 1.2.00: [campfire] merged from the old patcherMod file into the existing CD file
@group A
@commands Before the boot (pack that skipped 1.2.00): Compat file without `[campfire]` (or no Compat file), `config/creativeengineering-common.toml` with `[campfire] rainOutTicks = 120`, CD file present. Boot
@pass `[swaps] config sections [campfire] merged from creativeengineering-common.toml into creativedelight-common.toml`; CD file `rainOutTicks = 120`
@fails The fallback `mergeSections(OLD_FILE ...)` in `CreativeDelight` ran before the Compat one, or `campfireCarried` was true
@from batches/r1113/c2_l1.qb
bootexpect \[swaps\] config sections \[campfire\] merged from creativeengineering-common.toml into creativedelight-common.toml
bootreject \[campfire\] carried over from creativecompat-common.toml
shell grep -nE "^\[campfire\]|rainOutTicks *=" config/creativedelight-common.toml
look CD file [campfire] rainOutTicks = 120

## SQ-CFR-05 | rain douses an open-sky campfire on stone only
@group A
@commands Default config. `/weather rain`; `/setblock` stone, a lit `minecraft:campfire` on it under open sky; second lit campfire on `minecraft:coal_block`; a lit `minecraft:soul_campfire` on stone; a lit campfire on stone under a 3-block roof; wait 200 ticks; `/data get block` / block state of each
@pass Only the open-sky one on stone is `lit=false` (after 160 ticks; fizz sound, food on it stays); coal-block, soul and roofed ones stay `lit=true`; `/weather clear` + relight: stays lit
@fails `CampfireRain` not ticking (mixin not applied) or `CDConfig.CAMPFIRE` not read; tags `#creativeengineering:campfire/rain_douses` / `rain_proof_fuel` (blocktags.js)
@reviewed 2026-11-16
@from batches/r1106spf/b1.qb
> fill 90 -61 -40 100 -61 -30 minecraft:stone
> setblock 90 -60 -40 minecraft:campfire[lit=true]
> setblock 93 -61 -40 minecraft:coal_block
> setblock 93 -60 -40 minecraft:campfire[lit=true]
> setblock 96 -60 -40 minecraft:soul_campfire[lit=true]
> setblock 99 -60 -40 minecraft:campfire[lit=true]
> fill 98 -57 -41 100 -57 -39 minecraft:stone
> weather rain
> cdevtest tickwarp 220
waitlog verb=tickwarp end=\S+ ticks=220 60
> execute if block 90 -60 -40 minecraft:campfire[lit=false]
> execute if block 93 -60 -40 minecraft:campfire[lit=true]
> execute if block 96 -60 -40 minecraft:soul_campfire[lit=true]
> execute if block 99 -60 -40 minecraft:campfire[lit=true]
count Test passed == 4
> execute if block -25 -60 -35 minecraft:campfire[lit=false]
> weather clear
look the fixture campfire (open sky, grass) also out: SQ-SPF-81 thunder half

## SQ-CFR-06 | rainDouses = false: open-sky campfire stays lit
@group A
@commands `qrun.py toml` CD `[campfire] rainDouses = false`, reboot; repeat the open-sky campfire of CFR-05
@pass Stays lit after 400 ticks
@fails `rainDouses` read from the wrong spec (Compat)
@reviewed 2026-11-16
@from batches/r1106spf/b1c.qb passed
> setblock 90 -60 -44 minecraft:campfire[lit=true]
> weather rain
> cdevtest tickwarp 400
waitlog verb=tickwarp end=\S+ ticks=400 60
> execute if block 90 -60 -44 minecraft:campfire[lit=true]
expect Test passed
> weather clear

## SQ-CFR-07 | comfort near a campfire (default config)
@group A
@commands Default config. Bot player 2 blocks from a lit campfire, wait 40 ticks, `/data get entity <bot> ActiveEffects`; move the bot 6 blocks away, wait 120 ticks; `qrun.py toml` CD `[campfire] useComfort = false`, reboot, repeat at 2 blocks
@pass Near: `farmersdelight:comfort` with 3 to 5 s left; far: none after it runs out; `useComfort = false`: `minecraft:regeneration`
@fails `CampfireComfort.tick` not called, or the effect lookup (`farmersdelight:comfort` registry)
@from batches/r1106spf/b1.qb
> setblock 90 -60 -20 minecraft:campfire[lit=true]
> effect clear qa
> tp qa 92 -60 -20
sleep 3
> data get entity qa ActiveEffects
expect farmersdelight:comfort|Id:
> tp qa 96 -60 -20
> effect clear qa
sleep 7
> data get entity qa ActiveEffects
> tp qa -20 -60 -24
look near: comfort 3 to 5 s left; far: none

## SQ-CFR-08 | damage tags: creativedelight:stoves
@group A
@commands Boot; `grep "\[damage-tags\] loaded" logs/latest.log`; `grep -i "creativedelight:stoves" logs/latest.log`; probe (server script, `/reload`): `DamageTags.is(new DamageSource('endersdelight.endstone_stove'), 'creativecommon:fire')` and the same for `creativecommon:burn_tick`
@pass Loaded line lists `creativedelight:stoves(1)`; no "neither a built-in flag tag nor defined by any pack" WARN for it; with patcherMod 1.1.09 or later both probes are true (with 1.1.08 also true, from the old direct entry)
@fails CD jar missing `data/creativedelight/damage_tags/stoves.json`, or patcherMod's files lost the include
@from batches/r1106spf/b1.qb passed
bootexpect \[damage-tags\] loaded.*creativedelight:stoves\(1\)
bootreject neither a built-in flag tag nor defined by any pack.*creativedelight:stoves

